+1. **`spec/support/factory_optimization.rb`** (new, scoped helper):
+   ```ruby
+   module FactoryOptimization
+     def self.skip_side_effects?(transient_opt_in: nil, tag_opt_in: nil)
+       return false if transient_opt_in
+       return false unless defined?(RSpec) && RSpec.respond_to?(:current_example)
+       example = RSpec.current_example
+       return false if example.nil?
+       return false unless [:model, :request].include?(example.metadata[:type])
+       return false if tag_opt_in && example.metadata[tag_opt_in]
+       return false if example.metadata[:with_factory_side_effects]
+       true
+     end
+     def self.skip_bookmark?(transients) ... end
+     def self.skip_login_activities?(transients) ... end
+   end
+   ```
+   Loaded via `rails_helper` `spec/support/**/*.rb` before lazy `load_definitions`, available in callbacks (callbacks run during tests). Returns `false` (preserve old behavior) for other types, outside RSpec, or on error.
